\b Jarvis v0.1 - first setup and privacy boundary\b0\par
\par
Supported platform: Windows 11 x64 desktop editions only. Other platforms are not claimed as compatible.\par
\par
Jarvis is local-first and does not use a project-operated cloud backend. Supervision stops when this PC is off, asleep, offline where an external action is required, or Jarvis Core is not running.\par
\par
The local SQLite database is stored under the current Windows user profile and is not application-encrypted. Anyone able to read that Windows account's files may read it. Enable Windows device encryption or BitLocker when appropriate.\par
\par
Setup recommends starting Jarvis when you sign in. The optional feature is selected by default and can be cleared on the next screen or disabled later. At sign-in, Jarvis Core starts first and opens Jarvis Desktop. Closing the Desktop window hides it; full product exit is a separate confirmed action.\par
\par
Ordinary uninstall removes program files, Start Menu entries, and the login startup entry. It keeps the local SQLite database, settings, local password-protected backup files, and Jarvis credentials in Windows Credential Manager so reinstall can continue. Permanent deletion is a separate twice-confirmed operation. Jarvis never calls the Baidu API or deletes cloud copies during uninstall.\par
